all abandonment."], [0, "A new AI hub is coming to Europe as Google plans an AI center in Berlin to boost cloud computing, data infrastructure, and collaboration spaces for startups and research centers. This move sits within a broader push for digital sovereignty in Europe, aiming to support European firms as regional champions while managing dependence on US technology."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["News & Politics"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["gpt models", "ai benchmarks", "context window", "token efficiency", "hallucination reduction", "pentagon contract", "ethics backlash", "enterprise ai adoption", "financial institutions", "due diligence", "aws connect", "healthcare automation", "auditability", "hipaa compliance", "medical coding", "cloud computing", "digital sovereignty", "startup ecosystem"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778702401.9079592, "duration_sec": 5.2911553382873535, "validator_hotkey": "5DkzbwTnocecNohGP4aNVcHZfUgx8uA1MGQ4WB1u3kfi78gE", "task_type": "named_entities_extraction", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "named_entities_extraction", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "document", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "September 24, 2025\nA regular meeting of the City Council of the City of Boston was held in the Christopher A. Iannella\nChamber, City Hall on Wednesday, September 24, 2025, at 12:03 P.M.\nPresident Louijeune in the Chair. Present Councilors Breadon, Coletta Zapata, Durkan, FitzGerald,\nFlynn, Mejia, Murphy, Pep\u00e9n, Santana, and Weber. Absent Councilor Worrell.\nReverend Father Alexandros Pretorian of St. Nectarios Greek Orthodox Church, delivered the\ninvocation, and the meeting was opened with the pledge of allegiance.\nThe Chair moved to adopt the minutes from the September 17, 2025 City Council Meeting.\nMotion prevailed.\n_________________________________________________________________________\n1690 Message and order for your approval an Order authorizing the City of\nBoston to appropriate the amount of Two Million Five Hundred Thousand\nDollars ($2,500,000.00) for the purpose of paying the cost of a feasibility\nstudy and schematic design associated with a project for the Ruth Batson\nAcademy,"]], "participants": null}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "ner_001", "crc": 1321322, "title": "Extract named entities from documents", "name": "extract_named_entities", "description": "Identifies and extracts named entities from provided documents.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "ner", "prompt_template": "Extract all named entities from the provided document. Include the following entity types: PERSON, ORGANIZATION, LOCATION, and any other relevant entities. Return as comma-delimited list of