I was in there from the beginning, but I totally lied because I was there when there was maybe like a couple, maybe 200 people, like the first big group."], [0, "An early adopter. Yeah, that was probably like when we officially launched it. It really we started inviting people, like I said, I think in May of 2022, but then launched it like after that, kind of after the summer officially to kind of see how it would go. Yeah, Ashley, go ahead. It's a question for you, Kimberly. As a early adopter of this group, do you also have a hat?"], [0, "I actually don't have a hat, Kimberly. We must correct this. I do not have a Basecamp community hat. For those of you who are listening and not watching, Marissa has a Basecamp community hat. And I feel like I need to get one of those. We'll have to send you one. We don't want you to be left out."], [0, "So you guys tell me this because I can imagine someone who's listening who has their own product or service or business might be thinking like, what are the things I should consider if I want to start something like this? Are there things that we've learned from like, oh, we should never do that again? Like that was a mistake. Are there anything like that that you can share that maybe we've learned over time about how the Basecamp community works? Yeah."], [0, "I have an important thing to start with that really just harkens back to what was already said. And it's about the culture of it. And if you start with a basis of it's okay to try things, then it makes it literally significantly easier to have fewer nerves about what it is you want to try. As long as you kind of figure out what good measurement looks like, and that can truly just be qualitative or like a feeling more than anything else. Whatever the company values, however you can kind of"], [0, "prove that something is working and again it could just be a feeling i think that is an important place to start"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_